From: Darick Carpenter <carpenterd@byui.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] rtnl: receive whole netlink messages

netlink_event() read into a 4096-byte buffer and never checked for
truncation. A dump packs several messages into one, sized by the kernel
at NLMSG_GOODSIZE (8 KiB less overhead when pages are over 8 KiB) or the
largest receive buffer seen, capped at SKB_WITH_OVERHEAD(32768). On the
Raspberry Pi 5's 16 KiB-page kernel the initial link dump of lo, eth0,
can0 and wlan0 did not fit: wlan0 was cut off unseen, connman never
created its device, and "connmanctl scan wifi" answered "Not
implemented" until wlan0 changed state.

Read into 32768 bytes, which holds any message the kernel sends.

Kernel references: include/linux/netlink.h (NLMSG_GOODSIZE),
net/netlink/af_netlink.c (netlink_recvmsg, netlink_dump), checked in the
kernel source this image is built from (CONFIG_PAGE_SIZE_16KB=y).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Darick Carpenter <carpenterd@byui.edu>
---
--- a/src/rtnl.c
+++ b/src/rtnl.c
@@ -1472,7 +1472,15 @@
 
 static gboolean netlink_event(GIOChannel *chan, GIOCondition cond, gpointer data)
 {
-	unsigned char buf[4096];
+	/*
+	 * Large enough for any netlink message the kernel sends. A dump packs
+	 * several messages into one, up to NLMSG_GOODSIZE (8 KiB less overhead
+	 * with pages over 8 KiB) or the largest receive buffer seen, capped at
+	 * SKB_WITH_OVERHEAD(32768). With 4096 bytes the rest of a larger dump
+	 * message was cut off unseen, so on a 16 KiB-page kernel the initial
+	 * link dump lost interfaces (wlan0 on the Raspberry Pi 5).
+	 */
+	unsigned char buf[32768];
 	struct sockaddr_nl nladdr;
 	socklen_t addr_len = sizeof(nladdr);
 	ssize_t status;
